WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.512 --> 00:00:03.095
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:08.991
- [Narrator] It's 1991, and the world

00:00:08.991 --> 00:00:11.271
is introduced to a new TV show.

00:00:11.271 --> 00:00:12.731
It's about two brothers,

00:00:12.731 --> 00:00:14.314
with the same name.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.733
Pete and Pete was an
absurdist, surreal show

00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:22.374
shot in a very ordinary
looking suburb in New Jersey.

00:00:22.374 --> 00:00:23.816
- We're here in the site of the old

00:00:23.816 --> 00:00:25.692
Pete and Pete house from season two.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.664
I'm Michael Maronna, and I played big Pete.

00:00:27.664 --> 00:00:29.977
- And I'm Danny Tamberelli,
and I played little Pete.

00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:31.832
- [Michael] We haven't
been here in 20 plus years

00:00:31.832 --> 00:00:34.049
and it's, it's kind of a time machine.

00:00:34.049 --> 00:00:35.349
- [Narrator] This typical New Jersey house

00:00:35.349 --> 00:00:36.791
was the backdrop for the adventures

00:00:36.791 --> 00:00:39.458
of the eccentric Wrigley family.

00:00:41.482 --> 00:00:43.976
- Petunia was my beloved tattoo.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:45.844
Dance, señorita, dance.

00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:48.273
No one knows how I got it at age seven,

00:00:48.273 --> 00:00:50.095
and I believe when we did the shorts,

00:00:50.095 --> 00:00:53.714
it was on this arm and then at some point,

00:00:53.714 --> 00:00:56.471
it switched to this arm.

00:00:56.471 --> 00:00:59.300
I had to start showering with Saran Wrap

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.804
on my arm during the week because

00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:04.992
they didn't want to have
to keep touching it up

00:01:04.992 --> 00:01:07.137
and making it better.

00:01:07.137 --> 00:01:11.054
So, I had a stinky right
arm for three seasons.

00:01:13.719 --> 00:01:14.727
- [Narrator] One of the more bizarre parts

00:01:14.727 --> 00:01:17.741
of the show was Artie,
a reoccurring character

00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:20.211
who served as a constant
reminder to viewers

00:01:20.211 --> 00:01:22.745
that you can't always
ask for an explanation.

00:01:22.745 --> 00:01:24.283
- I believe that Artie was a figment

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:27.566
of our imaginations, but he
was a hell of a hallucination

00:01:27.566 --> 00:01:29.775
because even the adults
believed that he was there.

00:01:29.775 --> 00:01:30.843
(laughs)

00:01:30.843 --> 00:01:31.676
- True.

00:01:31.676 --> 00:01:33.077
(laughs)

00:01:33.077 --> 00:01:36.743
Artie is, of course, the
strongest man in the world.

00:01:36.743 --> 00:01:39.540
- Artie, the strongest man.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.247
- [Danny] He moved the
foundation of our house,

00:01:41.247 --> 00:01:42.435
- [Michael] an inch to the left.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.608
- [Danny] He ran very fast.

00:01:43.608 --> 00:01:46.996
- [Michael] He's eaten
several origami stars

00:01:46.996 --> 00:01:48.270
that were headed for his head.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.502
- I mean, who wouldn't want to have

00:01:49.502 --> 00:01:52.453
a personal superhero
with them at all times,

00:01:52.453 --> 00:01:54.159
as your best friend?

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:55.196
I would.

00:01:55.196 --> 00:01:56.029
I had it.

00:01:56.029 --> 00:01:59.362
- Artie, the strongest man in the world.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.744
- We are not brothers biologically.

00:02:02.744 --> 00:02:04.030
- We are fake TV brothers.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.032
Food poisoning?

00:02:05.032 --> 00:02:06.699
That's a triple u-ey

00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:11.063
- Unusual, unpredictable, undetectable.

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.791
- I didn't hang out with Dan much

00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:15.354
in the years immediately
following Pete and Pete.

00:02:15.354 --> 00:02:18.049
- We are brothers in a weird way.

00:02:18.049 --> 00:02:19.582
- Spiritual, we had a spiritual bond.

00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:20.962
- We do a podcast together,

00:02:20.962 --> 00:02:22.006
that's an important thing.

00:02:22.006 --> 00:02:23.350
- Dan and I record a podcast called

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.006
The Adventures of Danny and Mike.

00:02:25.006 --> 00:02:26.484
- So we see each other quite often

00:02:26.484 --> 00:02:29.651
and boy are we still fake TV brothers.

